      "summaries": {
        "en": "Chandra is an open-source OCR model designed to extract text from complex documents like tables, forms, and handwritten notes while preserving their original layout. It uses advanced vision-language techniques to understand document structure, enabling accurate text recognition even in irregular formats. Developers can integrate it via Python to automate data extraction from invoices, surveys, or historical records, making it practical for digitizing challenging documents.",
        "zh": "Chandra 是一个开源 OCR 模型，专门处理表格、表单和手写笔记等复杂文档的文本提取，同时完整保留原始布局。它采用先进的视觉-语言技术来理解文档结构，即使在格式不规则的场景下也能实现精准识别。通过 Python 集成，开发者可将其应用于发票处理、调查问卷数字化或历史档案转录等实际任务，为处理非结构化文档提供可靠工具。",
        "es": "Chandra is an open-source OCR model designed to extract text from complex documents like tables, forms, and handwritten notes while preserving their original layout. It uses advanced vision-language techniques to understand document structure, enabling accurate text recognition even in irregular formats. Developers can integrate it via Python to automate data extraction from invoices, surveys, or historical records, making it practical for digitizing challenging documents.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "chandra stands out for ai and ocr in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Chandra is an open-source OCR model designed to extract text from complex documents like tables, forms, and handwritten notes while preserving their original layout. It uses advanced vision-language techniques to understand document structure, enabling accurate text recognition even in irregular formats. Developers can integrate it via Python to automate data extraction from invoices, surveys, or historical records, making it practical for digitizing challenging documents.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/datalab-to/chandra for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
